<title>GREECE: GREECE TO TAX NEW GOV'T SECURITIES FROM JANUARY 1.</title>
<headline>GREECE TO TAX NEW GOV'T SECURITIES FROM JANUARY 1.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece will impose a 7.5 percent tax on interest earned from newly issued government securities, effective January 1, National Economy Minister Yannos Papandoniou told reporters.</p>
<p>Prime Minister Costas Simitis announced after a cabinet meeting on the 1997 budget that new T-bills and bonds would be taxed.</p>
<p>There have been widespread media reports in recent weeks that Greece would tax new state securities. -- Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
